        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Asphalt sealcoating is one of the best-value maintenance jobs around a house, as long as the pavement underneath is sound. It slows the oxidation, water intrusion and chemical damage that shorten asphalt's life, keeps the surface looking dark and clean, and costs a small fraction of an overlay or replacement. Use an asphalt-based product, fill cracks first, apply two thin coats in warm weather and reseal every two to four years.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Where the driveway is already failing, put the money into repair instead. And whether you do it yourself or hire a crew, the work that happens before the sealcoat goes on, cleaning, crack filling and oil treatment, decides how long the result lasts.
          </p>
